# Day 21 - Lists and Good Commit Messages

## 📚 Learning Objectives

* Learned ordered lists.
* Learned unordered lists.
* Learned list items.
* Learned how to write clear commit messages.

## HTML Tags Learned

### Unordered List

```html
<ul></ul>
```

Creates a bullet list.

### Ordered List

```html
<ol></ol>
```

Creates a numbered list.

### List Item

```html
<li></li>
```

Creates an item inside a list.

## Examples

### Unordered List

```html
<ul>

    <li>HTML</li>

    <li>CSS</li>

</ul>
```

### Ordered List

```html
<ol>

    <li>Study</li>

    <li>Practice</li>

</ol>
```

## Git Concepts

Good commit messages describe what changed.

### Good

```bash
git commit -m "Added learning technologies list"
```

```bash
git commit -m "Created daily routine page"
```

### Bad

```bash
git commit -m "update"
```

```bash
git commit -m "new"
```

## Practical Work

* Created ordered lists.
